# PR workflow (TrendPlan)

When the user says **PR** (or “create PR” / “open PR” for the current work), run this end-to-end unless they say otherwise:

1. **Sync main** — `git fetch origin main` and start from latest `origin/main`.
2. **Branch** — create a new branch with prefix **`feature/`** or **`bugfix/`** only (kebab-case slug from the change). No other prefixes.
3. **Upstream** — do **not** track `origin/main`. Prefer:
   ```bash
   git checkout -b feature/slug origin/main   # or bugfix/slug
   git push -u origin HEAD                   # sets upstream to origin/feature/slug
   ```
   Never leave the feature branch tracking `origin/main` (a bare `git push` would update main).
4. **Commit** — stage relevant files; commit with a concise message; author **habibullahm / mr.habiibullahm@gmail.com** (see github-commit-email rule). Do not commit secrets.
5. **Push** — `git push -u origin HEAD`.
6. **PR** — `gh pr create --draft --base main` (see **draft-pr** rule). Stay draft until the user reviews.
7. **Do not merge** — do not run `gh pr merge` unless the user explicitly asks to merge / mark ready and merge.

If there is nothing to commit, say so and do not open an empty PR.

Related: README **Branching strategy**; `.cursor/rules/draft-pr.mdc`.
